 \section{Audited Corpus and Curation Coverage}\label{sec:sadb_corpus}
 
-At the close of the campaign the working base held 957 records: 561 papers, 39 feedback-pathway records, 244 model records, 109 review records, and 4 recorder entries, 43 records below the laboratory's 1,000-record operating cap, with room to grow. Coverage of the retained papers is concentrated where the laboratory's design and experimental work needs it. Of the 561 retained papers, 523 carry curation notes, 426 carry animal-preparation tags, 240 carry notes assessing each paper's animal-study potential, 118 are linked to named feedback pathways, 86 carry an afferent classification, and 258 carry notes translating the paper's findings toward robot or simulation use; 550 carry DOIs, and 38 remain bare pending a findable text.
+At the close of the curation effort the working base held 957 records: 561 papers, 39 feedback-pathway records, 244 model records, 109 review records, and 4 recorder entries, 43 records below the laboratory's 1,000-record operating cap, with room to grow. Coverage of the retained papers is concentrated where the laboratory's design and experimental work needs it. Of the 561 retained papers, 523 carry curation notes, 426 carry animal-preparation tags, 240 carry notes assessing each paper's animal-study potential, 118 are linked to named feedback pathways, 86 carry an afferent classification, and 258 carry notes translating the paper's findings toward robot or simulation use; 550 carry DOIs, and 38 remain bare pending a findable text.
 
 The citation graph was built over the full audited corpus of 943 papers, which includes the 382 records the prune later removed and which the packaged database retains under an archived flag. Within that corpus, 730 papers are connected by 11,130 directed in-corpus citation pairs, and a Louvain community partition of the graph resolves 18 named topic clusters, from the classics of afferent locomotor control and spinal interneuron circuit modeling through human balance and posture to bioinspired flow sensing and deep-learning methods. The partition earned its keep in the prune: the satellite clusters it exposed, the flow-and-flight sensing, fish swimming, and neural-network method clusters, match the topic groups the first prune stage removed. The corpus, its citation graph, its cluster assignments, and the flat corpus export are distributed together in the packaged explorer, and Figure~\ref{fig:sadb_explorer} shows its table view as packaged.
